<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title><%= title %> - WMBS</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
  <style>
    .setup-steps { text-align: left; max-width: 32rem; margin: 1rem auto; }
    .setup-steps li { margin: 0.6rem 0; }
    .setup-url { background: #f0f4f8; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; font-family: monospace; word-break: break-all; margin: 0.5rem 0; }
    .setup-credentials { background: #e8f5e9; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; margin: 0.75rem 0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body class="error-page">
  <div class="error-box">
    <div class="auth-logo-wrap">
      <img src="/images/logo.png" alt="WMBS logo" class="auth-logo">
    </div>
    <h1>Setup required</h1>
    <p>Registration and Super Admin login will work <strong>after</strong> you run the one-time setup below.</p>

    <p><strong>Do this once (Render, no shell):</strong></p>
    <ol class="setup-steps">
      <li>In <strong>Render Dashboard</strong> → your service → <strong>Environment</strong>.</li>
      <li>Add a variable: Key <code>SEED_SECRET</code>, Value e.g. <code>wmbs2024</code> (any secret you choose). Save.</li>
      <li>Wait for the service to <strong>redeploy</strong> (automatic after saving env).</li>
      <li>Open this URL in your browser (replace <code>wmbs2024</code> with the same value you set):
        <div class="setup-url"><%= appUrl %>/api/setup?secret=wmbs2024</div>
        You should see JSON like <code>{"ok":true,"message":"Setup complete..."}</code>.
      </li>
      <li>(Optional) Remove <code>SEED_SECRET</code> from Render Environment and save again.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="setup-credentials">
      <strong>After setup, log in as Super Admin:</strong><br>
      Email: <code>superadmin@wmbs.com</code> &nbsp; Password: <code>SuperAdmin@123</code>
    </div>

    <p><strong>Option 2 (local):</strong> Run <code>npm run db:sync</code> then <code>npm run db:seed</code> locally with your production DB credentials in <code>.env</code>.</p>

    <a href="/auth/login" class="btn btn-primary">Back to Login</a>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
